 | 6 | 0.0 |", "textual_interpretation": "statistically significant heterogeneity, confirming that liquidity premium estimates varied substantially across the six regional markets examined", "interpretation_direction": "significant", "consistent": true, "notes": "Table row for Liquidity Premium Heterogeneity"}, {"test_type": "z", "statistic_value": 0.15, "df1": null, "df2": null, "reported_p": 0.8808, "p_equality": "=", "two_tailed": true, "raw_text": "| Publication Bias (Egger's Test) | Z-test | 0.15 | — | 0.8808 |", "textual_interpretation": "The Z-statistic Z = 0.15, p = 0.8808 was not statistically significant, suggesting the absence of systematic publication bias in the literature", "interpretation_direction": "not_significant", "consistent": true, "notes": "Table row for Publication Bias (Egger's Test)"}, {"test_type": "r", "statistic_value": -0.23, "df1": 191.0, "df2": null, "reported_p": 0.452, "p_equality": "=", "two_tailed": true, "raw_text": "| Bid-Ask Spread and Return Volatility | Pearson Correlation | -0.23 | 191 | 0.452 |", "textual_interpretation": "no statistically significant association between these variables", "interpretation_direction": "not_significant", "consistent": true, "notes": "Table row for Bid-Ask Spread and Return Volatility"}], "merged_tests": [{"test_type": "Q", "statistic_value": 23.04, "df1": 6.0, "df2": null, "reported_p": 0.0, "p_equality": "=", "two_tailed": true, "raw_text": "| Liquidity Premium Heterogeneity | Cochran's Q | 23.04 | 6 | 0.0 |", "textual_interpretation": "statistically significant heterogeneity, confirming that liquidity premium estimates varied substantially across the six regional markets examined", "interpretation_direction": "significant", "consistent": true, "notes": "Table row for Liquidity Premium Heterogeneity", "interpretations": [{"section": "results", "sentence": "The Q-statistic revealed substantial heterogeneity in reported liquidity premiums across markets, suggesting that regional institutional differences significantly influence asset pricing dynamics.", "keywords": ["substantial heterogeneity", "significantly influence"], "direction": "significant", "effect_strength": "strong", "hedging": false, "claim": "The Q-statistic showed substantial heterogeneity in liquidity premiums, indicating that regional institutional differences significantly affect asset pricing."}, {"section": "results", "sentence": "The Cochran's Q-statistic Q(6) = 23.04, p = 0.0 indicated statistically significant heterogeneity, confirming that liquidity premium estimates varied substantially across the six regional markets examined.", "keywords": ["statistically significant heterogeneity", "varied substantially"], "direction": "significant", "effect_strength": "strong", "hedging": false, "claim": "The Cochran's Q-statistic indicated statistically significant heterogeneity, confirming substantial variation in liquidity premium estimates across regional markets."}], "primary_direction": "significant", "has_cross_section_conflict": false, "any_hedging": false, "sections": ["results", "results"]}, {"test_type": "z", "statistic_value": 0.15, "df1": null, "df2": null, "reported_p": 0.8808, "p_equality": "=", "two_tailed": true, "raw_text": "| Publication Bias (Egger's Test) | Z-test | 0.15 | — | 0.8808 |", "textual_interpretation": "The Z-statistic Z = 0.15, p = 0.8808 was not statistically significant, suggesting the absence of systematic publication bias in the literature", "interpretation_direction": "not_significant", "consistent": true, "notes": "Table row for Publication Bias (Egger's Test)", "interpretations": [{"section": "results", "sentence": "The Z-statistic Z = 0.15, p = 0.8808 was not statistically significant, suggesting the absence of systematic publication bias in the li", "keywords": ["not statistically significant", "absence of systematic publication bias"], "direction": "not_significant", "effect_strength": "none", "hedging": true, "claim": "The Z-statistic was not statisti