."}}], "removed_records": [{"original_id": 1, "reason": "The proposed test's interpretation of the Q-statistic (Q(16) = 12.73, p = 0.009) as 'suggesting substantial homogeneity' is directly contradicted by the p-value, which indicates significant heterogeneity. The text states 'suggesting substantial homogeneity in treatment outcomes across diverse populations and therapeutic modalities. This finding supports the notion that intervention effectiveness varies considerably depending on contextual factors.' The p-value of 0.009 means significant heterogeneity, not homogeneity. Therefore, the interpretation is inconsistent with the statistical result.", "original_test": {"test_type": "Q", "statistic_value": 12.73, "df1": 16.0, "df2": null, "reported_p": 0.009, "p_equality": "=", "two_tailed": true, "raw_text": "Q(16) = 12.73, p = 0.009", "textual_interpretation": "suggesting substantial homogeneity in treatment outcomes across diverse populations and therapeutic modalities", "interpretation_direction": "significant", "consistent": true, "notes": "Heterogeneity in effect sizes across studies examining social anxiety interventions, N = 1,247 participants"}}], "added_records": [], "unmentioned_ids": []}, "predicted_tests": [{"test_type": "F", "statistic_value": 16.6, "df1": 5.0, "df2": 205.0, "reported_p": 0.001, "p_equality": "<", "two_tailed": true, "raw_text": "F(5, 205) = 16.6, p < 0.001", "textual_interpretation": "indicating that emotional regulation did not differ meaningfully across the experimental conditions", "interpretation_direction": "significant", "consistent": true, "notes": "Main effect of emotional regulation across age groups and intervention conditions"}, {"test_type": "Q", "statistic_value": 33.47, "df1": 18.0, "df2": null, "reported_p": 0.1, "p_equality": "=", "two_tailed": true, "raw_text": "Q(18) = 33.47, p = 0.1", "textual_interpretation": "demonstrating significant statistical heterogeneity across the literature. The non-significant p-value sugges